{"name":"Rich Brown","hex":"#715e4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rich","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wealthy: having a lot of money and possessions.","Having an intense fatty or sugary flavour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The rich people of a society or the world collectively, the rich class of a society.","(Can we verify this sense?)  the second placer in Tycoon"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rich Brown (blues musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Richard Brown, also known as Uncle Rich Brown, was an American musician and singer of spirituals and blues. He lived on one plantation near Sumterville, Alabama, all his life. John Lomax recorded him in 1937 and 1940 singing eleven songs, most of them spirituals. One of his most popular recordings was \"Alabama Bound\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rich_Brown_(blues_musician)"},{"title":"Modern English (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Modern English are an English new wave post-punk rock band formed in 1979 in Colchester, Essex, England. They are best known for their songs \"I Melt with You\", \"Hands Across the Sea\" and \"Ink and Paper\". The group disbanded in 1987, but re-formed two years later and then disbanded again in 1991. They reunited again in 1995 and have continued in various line-ups since then."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_01.jpg/330px-Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modern_English_(band)"},{"title":"Rich Brown (Michigan politician)","blocks":[{"text":"Rich Brown is the former clerk, former assistant clerk, and former Democratic member of the Michigan House of Representatives."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rich_Brown_(Michigan_politician)"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg/500px-Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg/1280px-Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg/500px-Modern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern English in 2012, left to right: Michael Conroy, Richard Chandler, Steven Walker","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModern_English_on_RealTVfilms_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Robbie_Grey_Modern_English_The_Saint_Asbury_Park_NJ_08232013R_LHCollins.jpg/250px-Robbie_Grey_Modern_English_The_Saint_Asbury_Park_NJ_08232013R_LHCollins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi